Q2. [sec_results.tex RE11]
BEFORE: The $\pT$ peak at ${\sim}\SI{0.6}{GeV/c}$ reflects the $Q^{2}\lesssim\SI{1}{GeV^2}$ momentum-transfer scale; the $\pPar$ peak reflects the medium-energy flux maximum.} \label{fig:xsec} \end{figure} \subsection{Comparison to the published measurement} \label{sec:results-compare} The published and unbinned results share the data and the flux, detector and generator systematics, and their cross-covariance is not available.
AFTER: The $\pT$ peak at ${\sim}\SI{0.6}{GeV/c}$ reflects the $Q^{2}\lesssim\SI{1}{GeV^2}$ momentum-transfer scale; the $\pPar$ peak reflects the medium-energy flux maximum. The vertical error bars on this measurement are the weight statistics of the reweighted simulated sample (the square root of the summed squared event weights, combined in quadrature with the bin error propagated for the completeness ratio, which is one by construction); they are neither the data's statistical uncertainty nor the reported covariance. Those on the published data (top) are the square roots of the diagonal of its statistical covariance. Horizontal bars span the bins.} \label{fig:xsec} \end{figure} \subsection{Comparison to the published measurement} \label{sec:results-compare} The published and unbinned results share the data and the flux, detector and generator systematics, and their cross-covariance is available.

